 notice="<h4>Notice (3 min)</h4><table class='tbl'><tr><th>Everyday</th><th>Abstract</th></tr><tr><td>People are poorer, and that worries me.</td><td>The <b>growth of poverty</b> worries me.</td></tr><tr><td>Technology develops quickly.</td><td>The <b>rapid development of</b> technology…</td></tr><tr><td>We must decide who is responsible.</td><td>The <b>question of responsibility</b>…</td></tr></table><p><b>Rule:</b> turn a verb or adjective into a noun (<i>develop → development, responsible → responsibility</i>) and connect it with <i>of</i>. Do not stack <i>of</i> more than twice.</p>",
 trap="<h4>Spanish-speaker trap</h4><p>Spanish forms these nouns easily (<i>el desarrollo de</i>). The common errors are the wrong preposition (<i>the importance <b>of</b></i>, not <i>for</i>) and the wrong form (<i>responsability</i> ✗ → <b>responsibility</b>).</p>",
